lor":"ccaaff","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-02-06T09:41:49Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T11:00:51Z","closed_at":"2025-02-06T10:59:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproductible in Godot 4.4.beta2.mono\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta2.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI have a player script in which I referenced a component responsible for flipping my player. In that ```flip_component.gd```, i've created a method called ``` force_flip(value: float) ``` to force player to flip when needed. I point out that this method does not exist in ```player.gd```\n\nInadvertently, I have written in a script this: ```player.force_flip(...)``` instead of ```player.flip_component.force_flip(...)```.\nThe bug i've faced is that Godot text editor does not display ```player.force_flip(...)``` as an error although it is not valid.\nSo the consequences of that is that I am only aware of that error when game's running\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate any 2d scene whereto you attach an script, and leave it empty.\nThen create a child node, attach a script wherein you reference parent node. Still in the child node, in its ```_ready()``` method, write for instance\n```parent_node_name.play_my_music()```. \n\nYou'll notice then that everything looks quite ok\nRun the game and see the result\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[godot_4.4.beta_2.bug_report.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18687772/godot_4.4.beta_2.bug_report.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"SilverWolveGames","id":92260598,"node_id":"U_kgDOBX_I9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92260598?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames","html_url":"https://github.com/SilverWolveGames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SilverWolveGames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102475/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102475/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}